# HavayarApp — Choosing how to implement a report

Pick **one** implementation path from the kind of report. Do not mix Stimulsoft into on-screen grids or dashboards.

| Kind of report | Implement as | Do not |
|---|---|---|
| **Tabular** (filterable grid, rows, Excel) | **Data Profile** (`system.SavedQuery`, `Type = DataProfile`) on a `<datatableprofile>` List page | Custom HTML tables, Stimulsoft, or a one-off grid page |
| **Charts / graphs / dashboard** (KPI cards, bar/line/pie, mixed summary + charts) | A dedicated **Report page** that uses the **existing ApexCharts** already in the panel | New chart libraries, Stimulsoft chart bands, DevExpress |
| **Print / official document** (certificate, form, printable layout) | **ReportBuilder + Stimulsoft only** | New C# report-rendering code, Crystal, DevExpress |

If a report is both a grid **and** charts on one screen, treat it as a **chart page** (see `CourseStatisticalReport`). If the user only needs a printable layout of the same data, add a Stimulsoft template **in addition** — do not replace the on-screen page with Stimulsoft.

## 1. Tabular → Data Profile

Follow `havayar-dataprofile-savedquery.mdc` (seed `SavedQuery` + `RoleAccess`, generators under `_tools/DataProfile/`).

- Prefer attaching the profile to the **existing entity List** page (`<datatableprofile entity-Type="typeof(Entity)">`).
- If there is no List page yet, add a normal List page per `havayar-add-new-page.mdc` and put the report columns in a Data Profile — not a custom `.cshtml` table.
- Excel export is the DataTable / Data Profile toolbar (`exportExcell`), not ReportBuilder.

Canonical seed shape: `Data/Scripts/Seed_SaleOrderDetail_DataProfiles.sql`.

## 2. Charts / graphs → dedicated page + existing ApexCharts

Copy the live pattern — do not invent a new chart stack:

| Piece | Canonical example |
|---|---|
| Controller (`Report` GET + `GetData` POST, `[ActionAccessItemType.Dashbord]`) | `WebApp/Controllers/Dynamic/Trn/CourseStatisticalReportController.cs`, `.../Pln/PlnTimelyDeliveryReportController.cs` |
| View | `WebApp/Views/Panel/Trn/CourseStatisticalReport/Report.cshtml`, `.../Pln/PlnTimelyDeliveryReport/Report.cshtml` |
| Library | `~/panelLib/plugins/custom/apexcharts/apexcharts.bundle.js` (already in the panel) |
| Create chart | `new ApexCharts($$('#elementId')[0], options)` then `.render()` / `.updateOptions()` |

- Filters, Shamsi dates, `$$.post`, `toastr`, and tab-scoped `$$` follow `havayar-js-jquery-conventions.mdc`.
- Do **not** add Chart.js, Highcharts, Google Charts, or another ApexCharts copy.
- Do **not** implement on-screen charts as Stimulsoft `.mrt` chart bands.

## 3. Print only → ReportBuilder + Stimulsoft

Use the in-app Report Builder (`/Panel/System/ReportBuilder`, `ReportBuilder.WebApp`). Data comes from a SavedQuery or `ReportBuilderTable`. Preview/print is opened with `appController.addPage(...)`, never `window.location`:

```javascript
appController.addPage('/System/ReportBuilder/ViewReportByName/' + templateKey
    + '?certificateId={\'values\':[\'' + id + '\'],\'condition\':\'=\'}&autoRun=True');
```

Entry points: `ReportBuilderController.ViewReport`, `ViewReportByName`, `StimulSoftViewReport`. Live wiring: `WebApp/Views/Panel/Trn/Certificate/ListByCourseId.cshtml`.

- Design the `.mrt` in the ReportBuilder Designer UI — **do not** write new C# that renders a report.
- Stimulsoft is **only** for print/official documents (certificates, signed forms, printable layouts). Not for List grids and not for dashboard charts.
- Font, RTL, and alignment of print text follow `havayar-stimulsoft-print.mdc` (canonical: edited `ProductionOrderForm`).

## 4. Must / must-not

| Do | Don't |
|---|---|
| Tabular report = Data Profile on a List page | Build a custom DataTable page "because it's a report" |
| Chart report = ApexCharts page copied from `CourseStatisticalReport` / `PlnTimelyDeliveryReport` | Use Stimulsoft or a new JS chart library for on-screen charts |
| Printable document = ReportBuilder Stimulsoft template + `ViewReportByName` | New DevExpress/Crystal/C# report classes |
| Add a menu entry to the Report / View action (or to the existing List page for a Data Profile) | Open print/report URLs with `location.href` |
